	"reverb_zones": {
		"_note": "One Area3D per structure body whose structure_type is listed in types (value = reverb_bus_amount, 0..1), built by MatchAudio once the map exists. Each box is computed at runtime as the union of the type's \"open\" volumes in data/maps/alesia_structures.json (never hand-copied), widened by padding_m on x and z only (the top stays at the roof underside) and lowered by floor_drop_m so sounds at foot level (steps, landings) are inside; it takes the body's transform. physics_layer is the one physics layer the zones use (layer 10 = bit 512; named here because project.godot is not touched); no gameplay query uses it, and every positional voice has that bit as its area_mask. The reverb follows where the sound is, not the listener. watchtower (a solid block, no inside), aqueduct_span (a raised span: a box would put reverb on pawns on top) and pediment_front are left out on purpose. Placeholders for Shibi (OQ-AUDIO-SPACE).",
